[00:00.10] The Story of the Joseon Dynasty
[00:02.12] The Lives of the King and the People
[00:04.42] A long, long time ago, in Korea, there was the Joseon Dynasty.
[00:09.48] Joseon was a very large country, and many people lived there.
[00:14.18] The Joseon Dynasty began in 1392.
[00:18.32] In this year, a general named Yi Seong-gye became the new king.
[00:22.36] Yi Seong-gye named the country Joseon.
[00:26.28] Joseon was an important part of Korean history for a long time.
[00:30.80] During the Joseon Dynasty, the king ruled the country.
[00:34.40] The king was in a very high position, and everyone respected the king.
[00:39.90] The king made the country's laws and protected the people.
[00:44.46] The king had to be smart and brave.
[00:47.66] The king could not do all the work alone.
[00:51.48] So, there were subjects (officials) next to the king.
[00:54.52] The subjects helped the king and ruled the country.
[00:58.34] The officials had to be smart and have a lot of experience.
[01:02.18] The people of the Joseon Dynasty lived while farming or making goods.
[01:07.42] Farmers planted crops like rice, barley, and beans.
[01:12.24] The farmers worked hard to feed and support their families.
[01:16.38] The people who made goods made things like clothes, bowls, and furniture.
[01:21.82] These people had good skills, and they made many good products.
[01:27.08] The people had to pay taxes.
[01:30.06] Taxes were necessary for running the country.
[01:33.54] Paying taxes was hard for the people, but they endured it for the sake of the country.
[01:38.98] In the Joseon Dynasty, there was a thing called social class (status).
[01:42.60] Social class was something that indicated people's social position.
[01:47.10] Royalty was the highest class, and the status lowered in the order of Yangban (nobles), Jungin (middle class), Sangmin (commoners), and Cheonmin (lowest class).
[01:55.14] The Yangban were people who studied a lot.
[01:58.74] They became government officials or scholars.
[02:02.22] The Jungin were people who possessed skills.
[02:05.58] Doctors, interpreters, painters, etc., were Jungin.
[02:09.90] The Sangmin were mostly farmers or merchants.
[02:13.46] The Cheonmin was the lowest class, and they did a lot of hard work.
[02:18.38] In the Joseon Dynasty, there were schools.
[02:21.40] At school, they taught reading and writing text.
[02:25.16] The children of Yangban went to school and studied.
[02:28.90] They studied hard and tried to become excellent people.
[02:33.52] The people of the Joseon Dynasty read many books.
[02:37.16] Books were an important method of gaining knowledge.
[02:40.78] Through books, people learned history, philosophy, literature, etc.
[02:45.98] During the Joseon Dynasty, many beautiful artworks were created.
[02:51.02] There were various artworks such as paintings, ceramics, and sculptures.
[02:56.08] These artworks show the lives and thoughts of the Joseon people.
[03:01.12] In the Joseon Dynasty, there were also major wars.
[03:04.60] The Imjin War (Japanese invasions) and the Byeongja Horan (Qing invasion) were major wars that occurred in the Joseon Dynasty.
[03:09.50] Because of the wars, many people died or were hurt, and houses and land were destroyed.
[03:15.38] However, the Joseon people fought bravely and protected the country.
[03:19.80] In the Joseon Dynasty, there were many excellent kings.
[03:23.26] King Sejong the Great created Hangul, and did many things for the people.
[03:28.66] Yeongjo and Jeongjo stabilized the country and developed the culture.
[03:33.52] Thanks to these kings, Joseon was able to develop further.
[03:38.00] The Joseon Dynasty continued for a long time, but eventually faded into the background of history.
[03:44.06] However, the culture and history of the Joseon Dynasty still give us a lot of influence today.
[03:50.16] While learning the history of the Joseon Dynasty, we can understand the past and receive help in living the present.
[03:57.50] The Joseon Dynasty was a very important era in Korean history.
[04:01.96] Various stories are contained within it, such as the lives of the king and the people, culture and arts, war and peace.
[04:09.04] Through the stories of the Joseon Dynasty, we can better understand Korean history and feel pride in our culture.
[04:17.40] In the late Joseon period, there were various changes.
[04:21.62] New technology came in, and commerce developed.
[04:25.66] The people's lives also improved little by little.
[04:29.48] But there were still many people having a hard time.
[04:33.10] They had to pay a lot of taxes, and sometimes bad officials tormented the people.
[04:38.50] Even so, the people did not lose hope and lived diligently.
[04:43.18] Helping each other, they overcame difficult times.
[04:46.76] In the Joseon Dynasty, there were special days.
[04:50.28] On Seollal (Lunar New Year), the whole family gathered, ate tteokguk, and gave New Year's greetings.
[04:55.02] On Chuseok (Harvest Festival), they made delicious food and conveyed their gratitude to their ancestors.
[05:00.94] On Dano, they washed their hair in iris water, rode swings, and spent an enjoyable time.
[05:06.96] Days like these gave great joy to the people.
[05:11.14] During the Joseon Dynasty, relations with foreign countries were also important.
[05:16.44] With China, they maintained a good relationship for a long time.
[05:20.48] With Japan, there were sometimes conflicts, but they tried to maintain peace.
[05:25.92] They also began exchanges with Western countries, but they were still cautious.
[05:31.02] The kings of the Joseon Dynasty made many efforts to rule the country well.
[05:36.40] They listened to the stories of the people and helped those in difficulty.
[05:41.08] They created new policies and tried to develop the country.
[05:45.46] However, there were times when kings also made mistakes, and they could not satisfy everyone.
[05:51.68] The people of the Joseon Dynasty lived diligently in their respective positions.
[05:56.44] Farmers plowed the land and planted crops, and merchants sold goods and left a profit.
[06:02.88] Technicians made good items and gave convenience to the people.
[06:08.30] Everyone worked together to build the country called Joseon.
[06:12.62] The Joseon Dynasty continued for over 500 years.
[06:16.10] During that long time, many things happened, and many people lived.
